From 697853d1c69760894ed0c69158b2afbddeb5e23c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StachowiakDawid <dawidos234@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:38:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: cs35l41, mfd: madera: Galaxy S10 TDM, calibration and
 sleep fixes

Codec side of the Galaxy S10 family audio (two CS35L41 speaker
amplifiers, CS47L93 codec):

 - cs35l41: set_tdm_slot, so that a machine driver can run the ASP
   with 32-bit slots carrying 24-bit samples.
 - cs35l41: the speaker protection calibration (CAL_R, ambient
   temperature, CAL_STATUS) is written after every DSP start with
   cal_apply=1, with per-amplifier CAL_R values (cal_rdc_right /
   cal_rdc_left, falling back to cal_rdc; cal_ambient); DSP
   hibernation at runtime suspend is optional (hibernate).
 - cs35l41: the CSPL PAUSE at stream stop is best effort. After a
   system sleep the firmware may not acknowledge it; the amplifier is
   powered down right after and the next start accepts RUNNING as well
   as PAUSED, so a missing acknowledgement is logged once and not
   returned as an error.
 - cs35l41: when the amplifier lost its supply in system suspend
   (detected through the reset default of IRQ1_MASK1), the probe-time
   init is redone, the register cache restored, the boost re-inited
   and the DSP firmware reloaded.
 - madera: pm_runtime_force_suspend()/resume() as system sleep
   callbacks. With runtime PM callbacks only, the PM core set the
   device runtime-active without powering DCVDD ("unbalanced disables
   for vdd_codec_1p2").

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/mfd/madera-core.c  |  10 ++
 sound/soc/codecs/Kconfig   |   1 +
 sound/soc/codecs/cs35l41.c | 273 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 sound/soc/codecs/cs35l41.h |  11 +-
 4 files changed, 287 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mfd/madera-core.c b/drivers/mfd/madera-core.c
index 2f74a8c644..c9ed4dbd90 100644
--- a/drivers/mfd/madera-core.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/madera-core.c
@@ -364,7 +364,17 @@ static int __maybe_unused madera_runtime_suspend(struct device *dev)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * With runtime PM callbacks only, the PM core treats the device as having no
+ * PM callbacks, enables "smart suspend" for it and marks it runtime-active in
+ * device_resume_noirq() without calling madera_runtime_resume(). DCVDD is still
+ * off then, and the next autosuspend disables it a second time ("unbalanced
+ * disables for <DCVDD supply>" after most system resumes). Real system sleep
+ * callbacks keep the runtime PM status and DCVDD in step.
+ */
 const struct dev_pm_ops madera_pm_ops = {
+	SET_SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(pm_runtime_force_suspend,
+				pm_runtime_force_resume)
 	SET_RUNTIME_PM_OPS(madera_runtime_suspend,
 			   madera_runtime_resume,
 			   NULL)
diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/Kconfig b/sound/soc/codecs/Kconfig
